abstract: >-
  Code and derived data behind a bibliometric and systematic review of 9,111
  articles published between 2010 and 2025 on the detection of structural
  breaks, change points and regime changes in financial and economic time
  series. Articles published in economics and business venues are analysed
  separately from articles on the same problem published elsewhere, and a
  rule-based screening validated on a double-coded sample separates the
  detection of breaks from regime-switching modelling.
keywords:
  - bibliometric analysis
  - systematic review
  - structural breaks
  - change point detection
  - Markov switching
  - regime switching
  - machine learning
  - financial time series
